IMPORT prelude

-- Part 8 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): documents provided under an Act (sections 51 and 52).
-- Section 51(5), the time at which service by post is taken to be effected, is encoded in sa-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part 8 -- Documents provided under an Act (sections 51 and 52)`

§§ `51 -- Service of documents`

-- src:549 | (1) This section applies if an Act or a legislative instrument requires or permits a document to be served on a person (whether the expression "serve", "give", "provide", "deliver" or "send" or any other expression is used).
@ref s 51(1) (src:549)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument requires or permits a document to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 51 applies` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument requires or permits a document to be served on a person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Way of serving a document on an individual` IS ONE OF
    `delivering it to the individual personally`
    `leaving it at the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind`
    `posting it to the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind`
    `leaving it at the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server`
    `posting it to the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server`
    `sending it electronically to the individual in a manner designated, or agreed to, by the individual for the service of documents of that kind`
    `another way of serving an individual`

-- src:550 | (2) The document may be served on an individual by—
-- src:551 | (a) delivering it to the individual personally; or
-- src:552 | (b) leaving it at, or posting it to—
-- src:553 | (i) the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind; or
-- src:554 | (ii) if such an address is not so designated, the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server; or
-- src:555 | (c) sending it electronically to the individual in a manner designated, or agreed to, by the individual for the service of documents of that kind.
@ref s 51(2) (src:550-555)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of serving a document on an individual`
      `the individual has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the document may be served on an individual in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
        WHEN `delivering it to the individual personally` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `leaving it at the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` THEN
            IF `the individual has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `posting it to the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` THEN
            IF `the individual has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `leaving it at the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server` THEN
            IF `the individual has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `posting it to the place of residence or a place of business of the individual last known to the server` THEN
            IF `the individual has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sending it electronically to the individual in a manner designated, or agreed to, by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another way of serving an individual` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Way of serving a document on a body corporate` IS ONE OF
    `leaving it at the registered office of the body corporate`
    `posting it to the registered office of the body corporate`
    `leaving it at another physical address designated by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind`
    `posting it to another physical address designated by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind`
    `leaving it at a place of business of the body corporate last known to the server`
    `posting it to a place of business of the body corporate last known to the server`
    `sending it electronically to the body corporate in a manner designated, or agreed to, by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind`
    `another way of serving a body corporate`

-- src:556 | (3) The document may be served on a body corporate by—
-- src:557 | (a) leaving it at, or posting it to—
-- src:558 | (i) the registered office of the body corporate; or
-- src:559 | (ii) another physical address designated by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind; or
-- src:560 | (iii) if such an address is not so designated, a place of business of the body corporate last known to the server; or
-- src:561 | (b) sending it electronically to the body corporate in a manner designated, or agreed to, by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind.
@ref s 51(3) (src:556-561)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of serving a document on a body corporate`
      `the body corporate has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the document may be served on a body corporate in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
        WHEN `leaving it at the registered office of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `posting it to the registered office of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `leaving it at another physical address designated by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind` THEN
            IF `the body corporate has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `posting it to another physical address designated by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind` THEN
            IF `the body corporate has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `leaving it at a place of business of the body corporate last known to the server` THEN
            IF `the body corporate has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `posting it to a place of business of the body corporate last known to the server` THEN
            IF `the body corporate has designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sending it electronically to the body corporate in a manner designated, or agreed to, by the body corporate for the service of documents of that kind` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another way of serving a body corporate` THEN NOTHING

-- src:562 | (4) A document is posted to an address by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter.
@ref s 51(4) (src:562)
GIVEN `the document is properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is prepaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is posted as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a document is posted to an address` MEANS
    IF `the document is properly addressed` AND `the document is prepaid` AND `the document is posted as a letter`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `52 -- Compliance with forms`

-- src:567 | If a form is prescribed or approved by or for the purposes of an Act or a legislative instrument, a form to the same effect is sufficient provided that deviations from the prescribed or approved form are not calculated to mislead.
@ref s 52 (src:567)
GIVEN `a form is prescribed or approved by or for the purposes of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form used is to the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deviations from the prescribed or approved form are calculated to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the form used is sufficient` MEANS
    IF NOT `a form is prescribed or approved by or for the purposes of the Act or instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (IF NOT `the form used is to the same effect` THEN NOTHING
          ELSE (IF `deviations from the prescribed or approved form are calculated to mislead` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE))

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `section 51 applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 51 applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the document may be served on an individual in this way` `delivering it to the individual personally` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served on an individual in this way` `leaving it at the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served on an individual in this way` `leaving it at the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the document may be served on an individual in this way` `posting it to the physical address designated by the individual for the service of documents of that kind` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
